  "discussion": "The pure PyTorch educational tiled implementation achieves exact mathematical equivalence with reference SDPA (MAE < 1e-5) while proving the memory scaling advantage of avoiding the O(N^2) attention matrix. As expected in educational Python implementations, runtime is dominated by Python loop overhead and lack of low-level GPU SRAM register tiling, whereas fused CUDA kernels (e.g. FlashAttention-2 / PyTorch F.scaled_dot_product_attention) fuse tiling directly into GPU shared memory."
